    "narrative": "With a sparse schedule on this September 10th, Ghost Ride the WHIP leans into the reliability of **Austin Riley**, who leads today\u2019s active lineup with a 64.26 score. Despite hitting seventh, **Austin Riley** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Martinez, who presents an xERA of 4.65, effectively offsetting the negative impact of his lower spot in the order. While **Isaac Paredes** (52.08) faces an uphill battle against the elite command of Wheeler, his placement in the three-hole provides a critical volume buffer for our RBI projections, and his positive platoon splits against right-handed pitching keep him comfortably above our 40-point floor despite the tough opponent.\n\n**Josh Naylor** rounds out the starters with a 46.48 score, narrowly avoiding a benching as he prepares to face the formidable deGrom. While the matchup against deGrom\u2019s 3.12 xERA suppresses his base projection significantly, **Josh Naylor** remains the superior play over **Cole Young**, who fell well short of our starting threshold with a 32.80 mark. **Cole Young** was the closest to cracking the lineup, but he was ultimately relegated to the bench due to a combination of park suppression and the heavy penalty associated with facing deGrom. We continue to monitor the status of **Corbin Carroll**, **James Wood**, and the injured **Tyler Soderstrom**, all of whom remain unavailable for tonight\u2019s action, leaving our bench core of **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana** firmly in standby mode to preserve our remaining game caps for more optimal matchups.",
